 piece to prevent endwise motion.","dna16":"8800118265001128","ex":[],"id":"wikt:ruff:noun:11","pos":"noun","src":"wikt","sym":"","syn":[]},{"def":"To shape (fabric, etc.) into a ruff; to adorn (a garment, etc.) with a ruff.","dna16":"8800118265001227","ex":[],"id":"wikt:ruff:verb:12","pos":"verb","src":"wikt","sym":"","syn":[],"tags":["transitive"]},{"def":"Of a falcon, hawk, etc.: to hit (the prey) without fixing or grabbing hold of it.","dna16":"8800118265001326","ex":[],"id":"wikt:ruff:verb:13","pos":"verb","src":"wikt","sym":"","syn":[],"tags":["transitive"]},{"def":"To ruffle; to disorder.","dna16":"8800118265001425","ex":[],"id":"wikt:ruff:verb:14","pos":"verb","src":"wikt","sym":"","syn":[],"tags":["rare","transitive"]},{"def":"A fish of species Arripis georgianus, found in cool waters off the southern coast of Australia","dna16":"8800118265001524","ex":[],"id":"wikt:ruff:noun:15","pos":"noun","src":"wikt","sym":"","syn":[]},{"def":"To play a trump card to a trick when unable to follow suit (that is, when unable to play a card of the same suit as the previous or leading card).","dna16":"8800118265001623","ex":[],"id":"wikt:ruff:verb:16","pos":"verb","src":"wikt","sym":"2:1,4:2,60:1,125:1","syn":["trump"],"tags":["ambitransitive"]},{"def":"Especially in the form ruff out: to defeat (a card, etc.) by ruffing, thus establishing the master card in the suit led.","dna16":"8800118265001722","ex":[],"id":"wikt:ruff:verb:17","pos":"verb","src":"wikt","sym":"","syn":["trump"],"tags":["transitive"]},{"def":"An instance of ruffing, or an opportunity to ruff, when unable to follow suit.","dna16":"8800118265001821","ex":[],"id":"wikt:ruff:noun:18","pos":"noun","src":"wikt","sym":"4:1,38:1","syn":[]},{"def":"A low, vibrating beat of a drum, quieter than a roll; a ruffle.","dna16":"8800118265001920","ex":[],"id":"wikt:ruff:noun:19","pos":"noun","src":"wikt","sym":"17:1","syn":[],"tags":["often"]},{"def":"To beat a ruff or ruffle, as on a drum.","dna16":"8800118265002027","